 "about": "Laurel forest of Madeira laurel, til, vinhático and barbusano with faya; planted eucalyptus, maritime pine, Japanese cedar and sweet chestnut on the mid slopes, canary palms by the villages; tree heath and Madeira bilberry in the heath belt up to the summits, broom, gorse and pride of Madeira on the ridge and the Paul da Serra, fish-stunning spurge on the coastal cliffs; bracken on the moor, chain fern under the laurels, agapanthus on the verges; brown cattle and a few sheep on the Paul da Serra, goats on the cliffs; white and pastel houses with orange tile roofs. Bananas and vines on the low terraces have no model yet, so the pack's broadleaves stand in the orchards.",
